IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain

-- g5-withdrawal.l4: Chapter 5, Subchapter B of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or
-- Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025: ss.39 and 40 (the revocation or suspension of the authorisation of a
-- tester or expert, with the cure-first rule; and the equation of testers and experts with State employees).
--
-- Written by ENCODER G5.  Imports only prelude, daydate, il-interpretation-time and domain.  Inputs: which of the
-- five grounds exist, whether a written hearing was given, whether the Minister demanded compliance or
-- correction and in what time, whether it was met, whether meeting it is impossible, and the Minister's periods
-- of suspension.  The Minister's power is a MAY rule guarded by the conditions; the bar of s.39(b) is a SHANT rule.
--
-- Periods met here: P24, the period for which the Minister suspends an authorisation (s.39(a)), kind V, s.10(c)
-- not applied (fork F-P24); P25, the time the Minister directs for meeting a condition or correcting a defect
-- (s.39(b)), kind D (a deadline for doing something) fixed by an official, s.10(c) applied (fork F-P25).  Both
-- lengths are the Minister's: an input, as a number of days, months or years from the day of the suspension or of
-- the demand, or as a last day.  The alternatives are callable.  A last day the Minister names is a date, not a
-- counted period, and s.10(c) does not move it.

§ `Chapter 5, Subchapter B: withdrawing an authorisation, and the status of testers and experts`

§§ `Nouns of ss 39 and 40`

-- The Minister's lengths (P24, P25), as he states them.
DECLARE `Period fixed by the Minister` IS ONE OF
    `a number of days fixed by the Minister`    HAS `the number of days set` IS A NUMBER
    `a number of months fixed by the Minister`  HAS `the number of months set` IS A NUMBER
    `a number of years fixed by the Minister`   HAS `the number of years set` IS A NUMBER
    `a last day fixed by the Minister`          HAS `the last day set` IS A DATE

-- s.39(b): the demand the Minister made, from the day he made it, and the time he directed.
DECLARE `Demand under section 39(b)` HAS
    `the demand was made on` IS A DATE
    `the time directed for meeting it` IS A `Period fixed by the Minister`

-- s.39(a) and (b): the grounds that exist and what the Minister did.
DECLARE `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` HAS
    `the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` IS A BOOLEAN                                 -- s.39(a)
    `the authorisation was granted on false or mistaken information` IS A BOOLEAN                                    -- (a)(1)
    `a condition for the authorisation under section 36 ceased to hold` IS A BOOLEAN                                 -- (a)(2)
    `a condition of the authorisation or an instruction under this Chapter was breached` IS A BOOLEAN                -- (a)(3)
    `special circumstances make the tester or expert unfit to be one` IS A BOOLEAN                                   -- (a)(4)
    `the work of the tester or expert is not done at a proper professional level` IS A BOOLEAN                       -- (a)(5)
    `the Minister demanded that the condition or instruction be met, or the defect corrected` IS A MAYBE `Demand under section 39(b)`   -- s.39(b); NOTHING if no demand was made
    `the tester or expert met the demand in the manner and within the time directed` IS A BOOLEAN                    -- s.39(b)
    `meeting the condition or instruction is impossible` IS A BOOLEAN                                                -- s.39(b), last words

DECLARE `Suspension under section 39(a)` HAS
    `the suspension began on` IS A DATE
    `the period of the suspension` IS A `Period fixed by the Minister`

-- The authorisation as the registers show it, for the status equation.
DECLARE `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded` HAS
    `the authorisation was given on` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the period fixed in the instrument` IS A DATE                       -- s.36(e); see g5-testing-bodies
    `the authorisation was revoked on` IS A MAYBE DATE                                   -- NOTHING if it was not revoked
    `suspensions of the authorisation` IS A LIST OF `Suspension under section 39(a)`

DECLARE `Enactment on which section 40 equates testers and experts with State employees` IS ONE OF
    `the Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979`                                      -- s.40(1)
    `the provisions of the Penal Law about public servants`                    -- s.40(2)
    `the Public Service (Restrictions after Retirement) Law 1969`              -- s.40(3)
    `any other enactment than the three listed`                                                      -- not listed

DECLARE `An act under sections 39 and 40` IS ONE OF
    `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert`
    `suspend the authorisation of a tester or an expert for a period`
        HAS `the period of suspension chosen` IS A `Period fixed by the Minister`

§§ `s 39 -- Revocation or suspension of an authorisation`

-- src:324 | {{ח:סעיף|39|ביטול הסמכה של בודק או מומחה או התלייתה}}
-- src:325 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} השר רשאי לבטל הסמכה שניתנה לבודק או למומחה או להתלותה לתקופה שיקבע, לאחר שניתנה לבודק או למומחה הזדמנות לטעון את טענותיו בכתב, בהתקיים אחד מאלה:
-- s.39(a): after a written hearing, the Minister may revoke the authorisation or suspend it for a period he sets,
-- if one of five grounds exists.  Lead-in: an opportunity to argue in writing was given (fact).
-- src:326 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} ההסמכה ניתנה על יסוד מידע כוזב או שגוי;
-- src:327 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} חדל להתקיים תנאי מהתנאים למתן ההסמכה לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 36|סעיף 36}};
-- src:328 | {{ח:תתת|(3)}} הופר תנאי מתנאי ההסמכה או הופרה הוראה מההוראות לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ה|פרק זה}};
-- src:329 | {{ח:תתת|(4)}} קיימות נסיבות מיוחדות שבשלהן הבודק או המומחה אינו ראוי להיות בודק או מומחה;
-- src:330 | {{ח:תתת|(5)}} עבודת הבודק או המומחה אינה מבוצעת ברמה מקצועית נאותה.
@ref s.39(a)(1) (src:326)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(a)(1), (4), (5) — a ground that the cure-first rule does not touch exists` case MEANS
        "(1)" ... case's `the authorisation was granted on false or mistaken information`
    OR  "(4)" ... case's `special circumstances make the tester or expert unfit to be one`
    OR  "(5)" ... case's `the work of the tester or expert is not done at a proper professional level`

@ref s.39(a)(2), (3) (src:327-328)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(a)(2), (3) — a ground that the cure-first rule governs exists` case MEANS
        "(2)" ... case's `a condition for the authorisation under section 36 ceased to hold`
    OR  "(3)" ... case's `a condition of the authorisation or an instruction under this Chapter was breached`

-- src:331 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} השר לא יבטל הסמכה ולא יתלה אותה, לפי הוראות סעיף קטן (א)(2) או (3), אלא לאחר שדרש מהבודק או מהמומחה לקיים את התנאי או ההוראה שחדלו להתקיים או שהופרו כאמור באותו סעיף קטן, או לתקן את הטעון תיקון, באופן ובתוך המועד שהורה, והוא לא עשה כן; ביטול ההסמכה או התלייתה יכול שייעשו בלא דרישה כאמור אם לא ניתן לקיים את התנאי או ההוראה שחדלו להתקיים או שהופרו.
-- s.39(b): the Minister may not revoke or suspend on (a)(2) or (3) unless he first demanded that the condition or
-- instruction be met, or the defect corrected, in the manner and within the time he directed, and the person did
-- not do so; no demand is needed if meeting the condition or instruction is impossible.  "And he did not do so"
-- is a fact about the time directed: it cannot be said while the time is still running, so the decision must come
-- after the last day of that time (P25, kind D, s.10(c) applied: fork F-P25; the alternative follows).
@ref s.39(b) (src:331)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand under section 39(b)`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 39(b) — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` demand MEANS
    CONSIDER demand's `the time directed for meeting it`
    WHEN `a number of days fixed by the Minister`   n THEN `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` n `days from` (demand's `the demand was made on`)
    WHEN `a number of months fixed by the Minister` n THEN `s 10 — the last day of a period of` n `months from the day` (demand's `the demand was made on`)
    WHEN `a number of years fixed by the Minister`  n THEN `s 10 — the last day of a period of` n `years from the day` (demand's `the demand was made on`)
    WHEN `a last day fixed by the Minister` lastDay   THEN lastDay

@ref s.39(b) (src:331)
GIVEN demand IS A `Demand under section 39(b)`
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 39(b), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` demand cal MEANS
    CONSIDER demand's `the time directed for meeting it`
    WHEN `a number of days fixed by the Minister`   n THEN `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `days from` (demand's `the demand was made on`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of months fixed by the Minister` n THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `months after an event on` (demand's `the demand was made on`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of years fixed by the Minister`  n THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `years after an event on` (demand's `the demand was made on`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a last day fixed by the Minister` lastDay   THEN lastDay

-- A demand was made, its time has run out, and it was not met: the first limb of the exception.  The person did
-- not meet it "in the manner and within the time directed", and the decision day is after the last day of the time.
@ref s.39(b) (src:331)
GIVEN met IS A BOOLEAN
      decisionDay IS A DATE
      lastDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(b) — the demand was not met and the decision is after the last day of the time directed` met decisionDay lastDay MEANS
        NOT met
    AND NOT `s 8 — the date` decisionDay `is up to and including` lastDay

@ref s.39(b) (src:331)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(b) — a demand was made, the time directed for it has run out and it was not met` case decisionDay cal MEANS
    CONSIDER case's `the Minister demanded that the condition or instruction be met, or the defect corrected`
    WHEN NOTHING     THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST demand THEN `s 39(b) — the demand was not met and the decision is after the last day of the time directed` (case's `the tester or expert met the demand in the manner and within the time directed`) decisionDay (`s 39(b), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` demand cal)

@ref s.39(b) (src:331)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(b), s 10(c) not applied — a demand was made, the time directed for it has run out and it was not met` case decisionDay MEANS
    CONSIDER case's `the Minister demanded that the condition or instruction be met, or the defect corrected`
    WHEN NOTHING     THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST demand THEN `s 39(b) — the demand was not met and the decision is after the last day of the time directed` (case's `the tester or expert met the demand in the manner and within the time directed`) decisionDay (`s 39(b) — the last day of the time directed for meeting a demand` demand)

@ref s.39(b) (src:331)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(b) — the cure-first rule is satisfied` case decisionDay cal MEANS
        case's `meeting the condition or instruction is impossible`
    OR  `s 39(b) — a demand was made, the time directed for it has run out and it was not met` case decisionDay cal

@ref s.39(b) (src:331)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(b), s 10(c) not applied — the cure-first rule is satisfied` case decisionDay MEANS
        case's `meeting the condition or instruction is impossible`
    OR  `s 39(b), s 10(c) not applied — a demand was made, the time directed for it has run out and it was not met` case decisionDay

-- s.39(a) and (b) together: the hearing; and a ground the cure-first rule does not touch, or a ground it governs
-- with the rule satisfied.  A person against whom (a)(2) or (3) exists and also (a)(5) can be reached under (a)(5)
-- without a demand: (b) bars only revocation "under (a)(2) or (3)".
@ref s.39(a), (b) (src:325-331)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39 — a ground exists that lets the Minister act` case decisionDay cal MEANS
        `s 39(a)(1), (4), (5) — a ground that the cure-first rule does not touch exists` case
    OR  (    `s 39(a)(2), (3) — a ground that the cure-first rule governs exists` case
         AND `s 39(b) — the cure-first rule is satisfied` case decisionDay cal )

@ref s.39(a), (b) (src:325-331)
@export Whether the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation of a tester or expert under s.39 of the Law: a written hearing was given, and one of the five grounds exists; for a ground that a condition or instruction lapsed or was breached he must first have demanded compliance or correction in a time he directed and that time must have run out without compliance, unless compliance is impossible. The time directed is counted with s.10(c) of the Interpretation Law
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` @desc Which grounds exist, whether a written hearing was given, and what the Minister demanded and whether it was met
      decisionDay IS A DATE @desc The day the Minister revokes or suspends
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday under any enactment, for the years concerned
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` case decisionDay cal MEANS
        "hearing" ... case's `the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing`
    AND "grounds" ... `s 39 — a ground exists that lets the Minister act` case decisionDay cal

-- Fork F-GROUNDS: the other reading applies the cure-first rule whenever (a)(2) or (3) exists, even beside another
-- ground, taking (b)'s "under (a)(2) or (3)" to reach every revocation where such a ground is among those present.
@ref s.39(a), (b) (src:325-331)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39, the cure-first rule applying whenever (a)(2) or (3) exists — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` case decisionDay cal MEANS
        "hearing" ... case's `the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing`
    AND "a ground" ... (    `s 39(a)(1), (4), (5) — a ground that the cure-first rule does not touch exists` case
                        OR  `s 39(a)(2), (3) — a ground that the cure-first rule governs exists` case )
    AND "cure first" ... (    NOT `s 39(a)(2), (3) — a ground that the cure-first rule governs exists` case
                          OR  `s 39(b) — the cure-first rule is satisfied` case decisionDay cal )

@ref s.39(a), (b) (src:325-331)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39, s 10(c) not applied — a ground exists that lets the Minister act` case decisionDay MEANS
        `s 39(a)(1), (4), (5) — a ground that the cure-first rule does not touch exists` case
    OR  (    `s 39(a)(2), (3) — a ground that the cure-first rule governs exists` case
         AND `s 39(b), s 10(c) not applied — the cure-first rule is satisfied` case decisionDay )

@ref s.39(a), (b) (src:325-331)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39, s 10(c) not applied — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` case decisionDay MEANS
        "hearing" ... case's `the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing`
    AND "grounds" ... `s 39, s 10(c) not applied — a ground exists that lets the Minister act` case decisionDay

@ref s.39(a) (src:325)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 39 and 40`
`s 39(a) — the Minister may revoke the authorisation of a tester or expert` case decisionDay cal MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert`
          PROVIDED `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` case decisionDay cal

@ref s.39(a) (src:325)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 39 and 40`
`s 39(a) — the Minister may suspend the authorisation of a tester or expert for a period he sets` case decisionDay cal MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `suspend the authorisation of a tester or an expert for a period` chosenPeriod
          PROVIDED `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` case decisionDay cal

-- s.39(b) as a prohibition: where the only grounds are (a)(2) or (3), revoking or suspending before the
-- cure-first rule is satisfied is forbidden.
@ref s.39(b) (src:331)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 39 and 40`
`s 39(b) — the Minister shall not revoke the authorisation on a ground that a condition lapsed or was breached before the cure-first rule is satisfied` case decisionDay cal MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    SHANT `revoke the authorisation of a tester or an expert`
          PROVIDED `s 39(b) — the grounds are only those the cure-first rule governs, and it is not satisfied` case decisionDay cal
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "s 39(b): the authorisation was revoked on a ground that a condition lapsed or was breached, with no demand for compliance having run out unmet"

@ref s.39(b) (src:331)
GIVEN case IS A `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation`
      decisionDay IS A DATE
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(b) — the grounds are only those the cure-first rule governs, and it is not satisfied` case decisionDay cal MEANS
        `s 39(a)(2), (3) — a ground that the cure-first rule governs exists` case
    AND NOT `s 39(a)(1), (4), (5) — a ground that the cure-first rule does not touch exists` case
    AND NOT `s 39(b) — the cure-first rule is satisfied` case decisionDay cal

§§§ `s 39(a) -- the period of a suspension (P24)`

-- P24.  The Minister sets the period (kind X, an input; kind V, a duration).  A counted period ends as
-- Interpretation Law s.10(a) (days) or s.10(b) (months, years) says, from the day the suspension began; s.10(c) is
-- NOT applied (fork F-P24); the alternative applying it follows.  The day the suspension began is a day of it.
@ref s.39(a) (src:325)
GIVEN suspension IS A `Suspension under section 39(a)`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 39(a) — the last day of a suspension` suspension MEANS
    CONSIDER suspension's `the period of the suspension`
    WHEN `a number of days fixed by the Minister`   n THEN `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` n `days from` (suspension's `the suspension began on`)
    WHEN `a number of months fixed by the Minister` n THEN `s 10 — the last day of a period of` n `months from the day` (suspension's `the suspension began on`)
    WHEN `a number of years fixed by the Minister`  n THEN `s 10 — the last day of a period of` n `years from the day` (suspension's `the suspension began on`)
    WHEN `a last day fixed by the Minister` lastDay   THEN lastDay

@ref s.39(a) (src:325)
GIVEN suspension IS A `Suspension under section 39(a)`
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 39(a), s 10(c) applied — the last day of a suspension` suspension cal MEANS
    CONSIDER suspension's `the period of the suspension`
    WHEN `a number of days fixed by the Minister`   n THEN `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `days from` (suspension's `the suspension began on`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of months fixed by the Minister` n THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `months after an event on` (suspension's `the suspension began on`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of years fixed by the Minister`  n THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `years after an event on` (suspension's `the suspension began on`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a last day fixed by the Minister` lastDay   THEN lastDay

@ref s.39(a) (src:325)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      suspension IS A `Suspension under section 39(a)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day` day `by` suspension MEANS
        day AT LEAST suspension's `the suspension began on`
    AND `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` (`s 39(a) — the last day of a suspension` suspension)

-- Fork F-START: the alternative begins the suspension the day AFTER the one it began on.
@ref s.39(a) (src:325)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      suspension IS A `Suspension under section 39(a)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(a), beginning the day after — the authorisation is suspended on the day` day `by` suspension MEANS
        day AT LEAST (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` (suspension's `the suspension began on`))
    AND `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` (`s 39(a) — the last day of a suspension` suspension)

§§§ `s 36(e) and s 39 -- when an authorisation is in force`

-- src:304 | {{ח:תת|(ה)}} הסמכה לבודק או למומחה תהיה לתקופה שיורה השר בכתב ההסמכה.
-- The status equation the Law implies but never states: in force from the day it was given to the last day of the
-- period the instrument fixes (s.36(e)), except from the day it was revoked on, and on the days of a suspension
-- (s.39(a)).  The day of a revocation or of a suspension's start is itself a day of the revocation or suspension
-- (assumed, not ruled: fork F-STATUS-DAY).
@ref s.39(a) (src:325)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      auth IS AN `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(a) — the authorisation was revoked on or before the day` day auth MEANS
    CONSIDER auth's `the authorisation was revoked on`
    WHEN JUST revokedOn THEN day AT LEAST revokedOn
    WHEN NOTHING        THEN FALSE

@ref s.39(a) (src:325)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      auth IS AN `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day under one of its suspensions` day auth MEANS
    any (GIVEN suspension YIELD `s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day` day `by` suspension) (auth's `suspensions of the authorisation`)

@ref s.36(e); s.39(a) (src:304, src:325)
@export Whether an authorisation of a tester or expert is in force on a day: from the day it was given to the last day of the period the instrument fixes (s.36(e) of the Law), except from the day it was revoked and on the days of any suspension (s.39(a)). The Law states no such rule in one place; this is the status the two sections imply
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      auth IS AN `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded` @desc The day given, the last day of the instrument's period, the day revoked if any, and the suspensions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` day auth MEANS
        day AT LEAST auth's `the authorisation was given on`
    AND `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` (auth's `the last day of the period fixed in the instrument`)
    AND NOT `s 39(a) — the authorisation was revoked on or before the day` day auth
    AND NOT `s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day under one of its suspensions` day auth

-- Fork F-STATUS-DAY: the alternative lets a revocation or a suspension take effect the day AFTER the day it is made.
@ref s.39(a) (src:325)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      auth IS AN `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(a), a revocation taking effect the day after — the authorisation was revoked before the day` day auth MEANS
    CONSIDER auth's `the authorisation was revoked on`
    WHEN JUST revokedOn THEN day AT LEAST (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` revokedOn)
    WHEN NOTHING        THEN FALSE

@ref s.39(a) (src:325)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      auth IS AN `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(a), a suspension taking effect the day after — the authorisation is suspended on the day under one of its suspensions` day auth MEANS
    any (GIVEN suspension YIELD `s 39(a), beginning the day after — the authorisation is suspended on the day` day `by` suspension) (auth's `suspensions of the authorisation`)

@ref s.36(e); s.39(a) (src:304, src:325)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      auth IS AN `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(e), s 39, a revocation or suspension taking effect the day after it is made — the authorisation is in force on the day` day auth MEANS
        day AT LEAST auth's `the authorisation was given on`
    AND `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` (auth's `the last day of the period fixed in the instrument`)
    AND NOT `s 39(a), a revocation taking effect the day after — the authorisation was revoked before the day` day auth
    AND NOT `s 39(a), a suspension taking effect the day after — the authorisation is suspended on the day under one of its suspensions` day auth

§§ `s 40 -- Application of laws`

-- src:333 | {{ח:סעיף|40|החלת דינים}}
-- src:334 | {{ח:ת}} בודקים ומומחים דינם כדין עובדי המדינה, לעניין חיקוקים אלה:
-- s.40: "testers and experts have the status of State employees" for three enactments, listed in (1) to (3): the
-- Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979, the provisions of the Penal Law about public servants, and the Public Service
-- (Restrictions after Retirement) Law 1969.  Their content is outside the sources; the status equation is
-- encoded, and the three items are the constructors of the list.  It reaches testers and experts only: not the
-- testing body, nor its employees who are neither.
-- src:335 | {{ח:תת|(1)}} {{ח:חיצוני|חוק שירות הציבור (מתנות)|חוק שירות הציבור (מתנות), התש״ם–1979}};
-- src:336 | {{ח:תת|(2)}} {{ח:חיצוני|חוק העונשין|חוק העונשין}} – ההוראות הנוגעות לעובדי הציבור;
-- src:337 | {{ח:תת|(3)}} {{ח:חיצוני|חוק שירות הציבור (הגבלות לאחר פרישה)|חוק שירות הציבור (הגבלות לאחר פרישה), התשכ״ט–1969}}.
@ref s.40 (src:334)
GIVEN party IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 — the party is a tester or an expert` party MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `a tester`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an expert` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref s.40(1), (2), (3) (src:335-337)
GIVEN enactment IS AN `Enactment on which section 40 equates testers and experts with State employees`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 — the enactment is one of the three listed` enactment MEANS
    CONSIDER enactment
    WHEN `the Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979`                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the provisions of the Penal Law about public servants`            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Public Service (Restrictions after Retirement) Law 1969`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other enactment than the three listed`                                               THEN FALSE

@ref s.40 (src:334)
@export Whether s.40 of the Law gives a party the status of a State employee for an enactment: testers and experts do, for the three listed enactments (Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979, the Penal Law's provisions on public servants, Public Service (Restrictions after Retirement) Law 1969), and nobody else, nor any other enactment, by s.40
GIVEN party IS A Party @desc Who: a tester or an expert is equated; a testing body or anyone else is not by s.40
      enactment IS AN `Enactment on which section 40 equates testers and experts with State employees` @desc The enactment asked about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 — the party has the status of a State employee for the enactment` party enactment MEANS
        `s 40 — the party is a tester or an expert` party
    AND `s 40 — the enactment is one of the three listed` enactment
